WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.775
Lash extensions need washing every day, but wash them wrong and they fall out fast!

2
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:10.968
Learn the right way to wash them, and why to avoid oil-based make-up removers.

3
00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:15.804
First: avoid oil-based make-up removers and creams around your eyes.

4
00:00:15.804 --> 00:00:20.456
Oil softens the extension glue, and your lashes fall out much sooner.

5
00:00:20.456 --> 00:00:25.746
Step one: wet your lashes gently and take a little oil-free lash shampoo.

6
00:00:25.746 --> 00:00:31.332
The soft foam lifts dust, skin oil and make-up from the base of the lashes.

7
00:00:31.332 --> 00:00:36.862
Step two: brush gently with a soft brush in the direction your lashes grow.

8
00:00:36.862 --> 00:00:41.448
No scrubbing and no pulling: about fifteen seconds per eye is enough.

9
00:00:41.448 --> 00:00:45.875
Step three: rinse with cool water and pat dry with a tissue.

10
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:50.905
Dry them on a cool setting from a distance, then brush your lashes back into shape.

11
00:00:50.905 --> 00:00:58.151
In short: avoid oil, wet and foam, brush gently, then rinse and dry on cool air.

12
00:00:58.151 --> 00:01:02.893
